<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 6 December, from 963 to 1921.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/papacy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/papacy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/963">963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,063 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leo VIII claims the papacy with the backing of Otto I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leo VIII, a Roman prelate appointed by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>, was ordained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and claimed the Holy See in opposition to John XII. The Catholic Church counts him an antipope until 23 June 964 and the legitimate pope thereafter.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1060 CE <span class="tih-ago">966 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Béla I is crowned king of Hungary at Székesfehérvár</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Béla I, who had rebelled with Polish help when his brother Andrew I named his infant son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> as heir, was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szekesfehervar">Székesfehérvár</a>, the coronation place of Hungarian kings. He reigned until his death in 1063.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bela-i-of-hungary">Béla I of Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szekesfehervar">Székesfehérvár</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1240">1240 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">786 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mongols sack Kiev</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a>'s army stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> after a siege, massacring much of the population. A traveller passing a few years later reported barely 200 houses standing; the city's ruin ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus</a> as a power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Columbus lands on Hispaniola</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a>, who had mistaken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, landed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> at a bay he named San Nicolas, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, and was welcomed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a>. The island became the first base of Spanish colonisation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1534">1534 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish conquistadors found San Francisco de Quito</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sebastián de Benalcázar's men founded the Spanish city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> on the site of an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> centre in the Andes. Its historic centre is today one of the best-preserved colonial cities in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1745">1745 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">281 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Jacobite army turns back at Derby</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Overruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart">Charles Edward Stuart</a>, his commanders began a retreat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a>, about 125 miles from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. The rising ended at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-culloden">Culloden</a> in April 1746.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edison records and plays back 'Mary Had a Little Lamb'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Edison spoke the nursery rhyme into his tinfoil phonograph and heard his voice played back. It was the first time a machine had reproduced recorded human speech.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Finland declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Finnish parliament adopted a declaration of independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, a month after the Bolshevik seizure of power. Lenin's government recognised it at the end of the month.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1921">1921 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">105 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Anglo-Irish Treaty is signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Irish and British delegates signed a treaty in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> creating the Irish Free State as a dominion, with Northern Ireland able to opt out. Divisions over it led to the Irish Civil War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
